#: ../../source/overview/index.md:1
msgid "What freeports is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/overview/index.md:3
msgid ""
"`freeports` turns financial reports published as PDF into tables you can "
"compute on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/overview/index.md:5
msgid ""
"Funds, and the companies that manage them, are required to disclose what "
"they hold, what their assets are worth, who manages them and how they "
"classify themselves under sustainability regulation. They do disclose it "
"— as an annual report, in PDF, laid out however the issuer's typesetter "
"chose. The obligation is on the *publication*, not on the *shape*, so the"
" same fact is printed in several hundred mutually incompatible ways. "
"Anyone who wants to compare across issuers has to read them by hand, buy "
"the data back from a vendor who read them by hand, or write a program per"
" issuer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/overview/index.md:13
msgid ""
"This project is the third option, made maintainable: an engine that knows"
" nothing about any particular report, plus **formats** — small, "
"separately maintained recipes, one per report layout — that tell it where"
" to look. The engine is the part that does not change; the formats are "
"the part the community grows."
msgstr ""

